meta {
  name: SearchMemory
  type: grpc
  seq: 2
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.KnowledgeService/SearchMemory
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "project": { "id": "{{projectId}}" },
      "query": "why the orders query is slow",
      "limit": 5
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  A search in the project's shared memory. With the embedding service on it is
  semantic (pgvector); without it, it falls back to the lexical trigram path — and
  the difference is declared, not silent.

  Isolation per account is a constraint: another account's memory does not show up,
  and the filter comes from the CONTEXT, not from the caller.
}
